# The edges of a paper's layout (#86), each one a reading once got wrong: hyphens inside
# a line ("pre- and post-training", "first- and") and at line ends (a compound,
# "multi-head", and a word, "sen-tence"); a sentence the foot of a column cuts, with a
# table and its caption at the top of the next; a paragraph whose first sentence starts
# at the foot of a page; a page whose text ends without a line break; and a page that
# is one figure, its axis labels set near the body size and a caption whose first line
# ends in a colon. The text is original. Rebuild the PDF with
#   swift scripts/make-pdf-fixture.swift fixtures/pdf/edges.layout fixtures/pages/edges.pdf
page
title Reading a Paper at the Edges of Its Layout
gap 4
center Lena Ortiz        Sami Okafor
center lena@unread.example
gap 18
column
heading Abstract
para
| A reader of papers meets the layout where it is
| least regular, from the head of a column to its
| foot. This one checks the joins a type-
| setter leaves behind and the blocks that stand in
| the way of a sentence.
heading 1 Hyphens
para
| Some checks run both pre- and post-training, and
| some on first- and second-order terms alike. A
| multi-
| head layout keeps its hyphen, while a sen-
| tence broken at its end is joined again. The
| checks we ran pre-
| and post-training agree.
heading 2 Tables
para
| Tables are set apart from the text around them.
| When a table stands in the middle of a sentence,
| the
column
row Viewer;Words;Lines;Figures
row WebKit;98.1;96.0;12
row Preview;97.4;95.2;12
para flush
| Table 1: Words and lines read whole, per viewer.
para flush
| reading finishes the sentence first and then
| announces the table.
para
| A paragraph that starts at the foot of a page
footer 36 1
page
header Reading a Paper at the Edges of Its Layout
column
| and goes on at the top of the next one is read
| as one sentence, without the page number.
heading 3 Figures
para
| A page that holds only a figure is announced, and
| its caption is read whole.
page
column
figure 60 Page;Lines;Words
labels 9.5 The;reader;keeps;its;place;on;the;page
row The;reader;keeps;its;place
para flush
| Figure 1: The words of a sentence drawn as a grid. Top:
| the words as set. Bottom: as read.
